+/*
+  streamingbox: improvements of the bitrate controller (environment SB_CTL, letters, default "" = original behaviour since sb8, "A" soft start)
+  A  (OFF by default since sb8: the bitrate starts at the maximum like in the original BELABOX) soft start: the encoder starts at 1 Mbit/s (or the maximum, if lower) and climbs, instead of starting at the maximum: at the maximum a
+     slow link is flooded for seconds before the controller reacts (SRT queues up, the picture stands)
+  B  the thresholds that depend on the SRT latency use at most 1000 ms of it: with a latency of 2000 ms the controller waited for 667 ms RTT
+     before it dropped to the minimum, the send buffer then held seconds of video
+  C  the bitrate is limited by what was really sent (like Moblin: sent + 1 Mbit/s or 1.7 x sent, whichever is more): the encoder must not run
+     away from the link when the picture is easy or the link just got worse. What was sent is the average of the last ~3 seconds (sb6): measured
+     over 100 ms, a pause of the picture (the pipeline holds for a moment, the cameras are late) counted as "nothing was sent", the cap fell to
+     1 Mbit/s and the bitrate dropped with it, again and again: it could not climb above 2-3 Mbit/s although the link was free.
+     OFF BY DEFAULT since sb7: even with the 3 s average the bitrate follows the picture, not the link. A still picture (a phone put down) makes
