+/*
+  streamingbox extension: dynamic feeds
+
+  The branch of a picture-in-picture / drone feed (rtmpsrc ! flvdemux ! decoder ! ... ! compositor) can be stopped and started
+  again while the stream keeps running. Without this a feed that disappears (an error of its rtmpsrc) ends belacoder, and
+  a feed that appears needs a new pipeline: the stream is interrupted for seconds in both cases.
+
+  The elements of a branch are named <feed>_..., <feed> is the name of the flvdemux (sbpd, sbdd), and the rtmpsrc is
+  <feed>_src. The first buffer pads of the flvdemux are linked to <feed>_vq (video) and <feed>_aq (audio).
+  A last line "#sb-absent: sbpd sbdd" of the pipeline file lists the feeds that are not there at the start: their
+  elements are kept in the NULL state.
+
+    feed <name> on|off     start / stop the branch (on: nothing happens when it is running already)
+
+  When a branch stops (an error of one of its elements, or "off") its picture is hidden, and the audio goes back to the
+  first pad of the input-selector "asel" when the audio of the feed was selected. The feed is aligned to the pipeline
+  clock again when it comes back.
